\label{def:4.8}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item A cap or a cup (decorated or not) is said to be oriented clockwise, if it is attached on the right side to a ${\mkern.5mu\begin{tikzpicture}[x=.27em,y=.45em,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.99 with {\arrow[black]{Stealth[length=4.8pt]}}}]
\draw[color=white,postaction={decorate}] (0,.1) -- (0,-.1);
\end{tikzpicture}\mkern.5mu}$, and is said to be oriented counter-clockwise, if it is attached on the right side to a ${\mkern.5mu\begin{tikzpicture}[x=.27em,y=.45em,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.99 with {\arrow[black]{Stealth[length=4.8pt]}}}]
\draw[color=white,postaction={decorate}] (0,-.1) -- (0,.1);
\end{tikzpicture}\mkern.5mu}$.
        \item The degree of an arc diagram is given by the number of clockwise caps and clockwise cups it contains.
    \end{itemize}

