    Let $\lambda, \mu \in \Delta_n^p$ be weights, and assume that $\underline{\lambda}\overline{\mu}$ can be oriented. Then there is an isomorphism of vector spaces
    \begin{align*}
        \varphi_{\underline{\lambda}\overline{\mu}} : {}_\lambda(\mathbb{D} _n^p){}_\mu &\longrightarrow \mathcal{M}(\underline{\lambda}\overline{\mu}) \\
        \underline{\lambda}\nu\overline{\mu} &\mapsto \prod_{C \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{clock}}(\underline{\lambda}\nu\overline{\mu})} X_{t(C)}
    \end{align*}
    where $\mathcal{C}_{\text{clock}}(\underline{\lambda}\nu\overline{\mu})$ is the set of clockwise oriented circles in $\underline{\lambda}\nu\overline{\mu}$, and $t(C)$ is the position of the rightmost arrow of $\nu$ which $C$ goes through.

