        where a nested surgery is a split surgery where both of the resulting components are circles one of which is contained in the other one.

        \textbf{Reconnect :} If the surgery produces two connected components out of two, which only happens if both are open arcs, then either the two lines (before the surgery) are propagating and we leave $y$ as it is, otherwise we multiply $y$ with $0$. We say that an open arc is propagating if it connects the bottom boundary to the top boundary (or vice-versa).
        \item If the resulting diagram cannot be oriented, multiply $y$ with $0$.
        \item We define $\chi'(f \otimes g)$ to be equal to the resulting polynomial $y$.
    \end{enumerate}
